<title>USA: EEP request still awaiting decision-USDA's Collins.</title>
<headline>EEP request still awaiting decision-USDA's Collins.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A proposal to subsidize sales of U.S. wheat flour and barley malt still needs a decision from an inter-agency panel, the Agriculture Department's chief economist said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;To my knowledge, that's where it still is,&quot; chief economist Keith Collins told reporters who asked about the proposal.</p>
<p>USDA has proposed making some of the $10 million alloted to the Export Enhancement Program, the major U.S. export subsidy program, in fiscal 1997 to aid sales of wheat flour and barley malt. The United States has not subsidized grain exports for two years.</p>
</text>
